# 221: calling a name that is neither one of the three builtins nor a declared
# function. Functions are hoisted (§2), so "declared further down" is not an
# excuse and the name really is unknown — `error.rs::undefined_function`, a
# `Name` error per §3. The line printed before it survives and the line after it
# never runs (§3: the output of lines 1..n, then the error).
--- source
print "before";
print nope(1);
print "after";
--- expect
before
error: Name at line 2: undefined function 'nope'
